// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: `mapIndexed` with an ALIAS literal-union result `U`, where the CALLBACK
// reaches the call site through a BINDING rather than by name. `vl check` exits 0, the module
// is written, and the engine refuses it at load —
//
//   (wasmtime) type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found i32
//
// THE AXIS IS THE CALLBACK'S SPELLING, which is the one the fix's own grid does not vary
// against an alias `U`. That grid has a row for "alias `U`, callback by name" and a row for
// "inline `U`, callback as a lambda"; the CROSS cell — alias `U` AND callback through a
// binding — is never taken, which is the module header's own lesson #2 ("the probe has to
// vary the dimension the claim is about") failing on the grid written to satisfy it.
//
// PRE-EXISTING, and the direction matters for the ledger. On the parent seed this cell is
// ALSO check-clean invalid wasm — measured, by building the parent compiler from source. What
// changed is its NEIGHBOUR: the by-name cell was an honest emit refusal there
// (`literal-union string widening with no members`) and runs now. So the RESULT-list fix moved
// one cell and left this one exactly where it found it. It did not trade a loud refusal for a
// silent miscompile, which is the reading the two cells invite side by side.
//
// THE HINT DOES NOT SIGNPOST IT. The sibling defect
// (`soundness/xfail-miscompile-fntype-litunion-result-call.vl`) is at least accompanied by a
// redundant-annotation HINT, which that file calls its only signpost. Here the binding needs
// no annotation to fail — `const g = base` and `const g: (i32, i32) => K = base` both do —
// so there is nothing to hint about.
//
// NOT COVERED BY THE "recorded rather than duplicated" POLICY next door. That policy applies
// to the same defect through a different spelling; this cell's rep direction is the MIRROR
// (`expected (ref $type), found i32` against that file's `expected i32, found (ref $type)`),
// so it would not go green with it.
//
// REMEDY: pass the function BY NAME. An INLINE `U` through a binding is unaffected.
// @hint Intentionally-unused parameter `_i`
import { mapIndexed } from "std:array"

type K = "a" | "b"

function base(x: i32, _i: i32): K {
  if x > 0 { return "b" }
  return "a"
}

const g = base
print([0, 1].mapIndexed(g)[1])
